{"name":"Silverton","hex":"#bfd9ce","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Silverton","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A placename:\nA small village west of Broken Hill, New South Wales, Australia.\nA locality in Yankalilla district council area, South Australia.\nA village in the Slocan Valley, British Columbia, Canada.\nAn eastern suburb of Pretoria, South Africa.\nA large village and civil parish in Mid Devon district, Devon, England . \nA large housing estate of Dumbarton, West Dunbartonshire council area, Scotland .\nA number of places in the United States:\nA statutory town, the county seat of San Juan County, Colorado.\nAn unincorporated community in Shoshone County, Idaho.\nA historical town in Douglas County, Missouri.\nAn unincorporated community in Ocean County, New Jersey.\nA city in Marion County, Oregon.\nA village in Hamilton County, Ohio.\nA small city, the county seat of Briscoe County, Texas.\nAn unincorporated community in Snohomish County, Washington.\nAn unincorporated community in Jackson County, West Virginia.","A small village west of Broken Hill, New South Wales, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Silverton"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silverton, New South Wales","blocks":[{"text":"Silverton is a village at the far west of New South Wales, Australia, 26 kilometres (16 mi) north-west of Broken Hill. At the 2021 census, Silverton had a population of 48."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Town_entry_sign%2C_Silverton%2C_New_South_Wales%2C_Australia.jpg/330px-Town_entry_sign%2C_Silverton%2C_New_South_Wales%2C_Australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silverton%2C_New_South_Wales"},{"title":"Silverton Wind Farm","blocks":[{"text":"The Silverton Wind Farm is a 199-megawatt wind farm situated on the southern end of the Barrier Ranges in New South Wales, north of Silverton, built for AGL Energy by Catcon and General Electric. Planning began around 2007, and the wind farm was finally fully commissioned in May 2020, following some setbacks due to grid issues after initial implementation in 2018."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silverton_Wind_Farm"},{"title":"Silverton (hotel and casino)","blocks":[{"text":"Silverton is a 300-room hotel and casino in Enterprise, Nevada, near the southern end of the Las Vegas Valley. It features a rustic lodge theme and a 65,556 sq ft (6,090.4 m2) casino.\nIt is owned and operated by Ed Roski Jr., and is located three miles south of the Las Vegas Strip. Roski purchased an 80-acre parcel in 1989, and originally planned to build an industrial warehouse on the site, before deciding on a casino instead. In 1993, he partnered with Boomtown, Inc. to build a hotel and casino on 56 acres of the property. Roski built the project through a company of his, with financing from Boomtown, Inc."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Silverton_Casino_Hotel.jpg/330px-Silverton_Casino_Hotel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silverton_(hotel_and_casino)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/SilvertonCrossroads.JPG/500px-SilvertonCrossroads.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/SilvertonCrossroads.JPG/1280px-SilvertonCrossroads.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/SilvertonCrossroads.JPG/500px-SilvertonCrossroads.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" The main crossroads in Silverton, with the Silverton Hotel on the right","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilvertonCrossroads.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Silverton_John_Dynon_Gallery-1_%2821182872998%29.jpg/500px-Silverton_John_Dynon_Gallery-1_%2821182872998%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Silverton_John_Dynon_Gallery-1_%2821182872998%29.jpg/1280px-Silverton_John_Dynon_Gallery-1_%2821182872998%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Silverton_John_Dynon_Gallery-1_%2821182872998%29.jpg/500px-Silverton_John_Dynon_Gallery-1_%2821182872998%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The John Dynon Gallery","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilverton_John_Dynon_Gallery-1_(21182872998).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/P1000583_Silverton_Mad_Max_Museum_Landscape.jpg/500px-P1000583_Silverton_Mad_Max_Museum_Landscape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/P1000583_Silverton_Mad_Max_Museum_Landscape.jpg/1280px-P1000583_Silverton_Mad_Max_Museum_Landscape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/P1000583_Silverton_Mad_Max_Museum_Landscape.jpg/500px-P1000583_Silverton_Mad_Max_Museum_Landscape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mad Max 2 Museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AP1000583_Silverton_Mad_Max_Museum_Landscape.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Las_Vegas._Boomtown_Casino_Hotel.jpg/500px-Las_Vegas._Boomtown_Casino_Hotel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Las_Vegas._Boomtown_Casino_Hotel.jpg/1280px-Las_Vegas._Boo